# Pairs with NoLostContribution. Reproduces production before #4618 was fixed
# (#4665): the resize's snapshot drain merges the source's row into the
# resized copy last-writer-wins, not as a join, so a resized copy whose own
# terminal fold already holds the saga's contribution keeps one copy and loses
# a non-atomic write only the source held.
MODULE: NoLostContributionResizeDrainLastWriterWins
TARGET: NoLostContribution
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the resize's snapshot drain merges last-writer-wins, losing a contribution only the source held
PERTURBS: Copy

--- FIND
    /\ Import
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT !["dst"] = @ \/ (pend["src"] /\ sg = "prepared")]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a resize's snapshot drain merges last-writer-wins.
    /\ IF kind = "resize"
       THEN IF stamp["src"] > stamp["dst"]
            THEN /\ row' = [row EXCEPT !["dst"] = row["src"]]
                 /\ stamp' = [stamp EXCEPT !["dst"] = stamp["src"]]
                 /\ clk' = [clk EXCEPT !["dst"] = Max(@, stamp["src"])]
                 /\ migd' = migd
            ELSE UNCHANGED <<row, stamp, clk, migd>>
       ELSE Import
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT !["dst"] = @ \/ (pend["src"] /\ sg = "prepared")]
--- END